l holes on the edges of the ivory suggest that it may have been one of the many Byzantine ivories used to decorate the covers of religious texts when these were later taken to the West.\",\"extendedStatuses\":[\"accessioned\"],\"gallery\":\"300\",\"geography\":[\"Byzantine Egypt\"],\"geolocation\":[],\"has3d\":false,\"hasImage\":true,\"hasNaziEraProvenance\":false,\"isHighlight\":false,\"isOnView\":true,\"isOpenAccess\":true,\"materials\":[\"Bone\",\"Ivory\",\"Plaques\"],\"medium\":\"Elephant ivory\",\"objectName\":\"Plaque\",\"period\":null,\"provenance\":null,\"reign\":null,\"sortArtist\":\"byzantine\",\"sortTitle\":\"panel with st peter or st paul\",\"suggestionArtists\":[{\"value\":\"Byzantine\"}],\"suggestionGeolocations\":[],\"suggestionMaterials\":[{\"value\":\"Bone\"},{\"value\":\"Ivory\"},{\"value\":\"Plaques\"}],\"tags\":[\"Saint Paul\",\"Saint Peter\"],\"thumbnailAltText\":\"Panel with St. Peter or St. Paul (?), Elephant ivory, Byzantine\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://images.metmuseum.org/CRDImages/md/web-additional/DT243375.jpg\",\"tmsDepartmentId\":347,\"title\":[\"Panel with St. Peter or St. Paul (?)\"],\"whenFrom\":500,\"whenTo\":599,\"yearsMinMax\":[500,599],\"yearRange\":{\"gte\":500,\"lte\":599}}}],[\"$\",\"$L38\",\"collectionObject-undefined\",{\"index\":1,\"enforceMaxWidth\":true,\"object\":{\"accessionNumber\":\"10.175.106\",\"artistPrimary\":null,\"artistSecondary\":[],\"artists\":[],\"artistsFlattened\":[\"Coptic\"],\"classifications\":[\"Woodwork-Architectural\"],\"culture\":\"Coptic\",\"crdCollectionIds\":[17],\"crdId\":473023,\"creditLine\":\"Rogers Fund, 1910\",\"dated\":\"6th–8th century\",\"departmentName\":[\"Medieval Art and The Cloisters\"],\"departmentSlug\":[\"medieval-art-and-the-cloisters\"],\"dynasty\":null,\"description\":null,\"extendedStatuses\":[\"accessioned\"],\"gallery\":null,\"geography\":[\"Byzantine Egypt\"],\"geolocation\":[],\"has3d\":false,\"hasImage\":true,\"hasNaziEraProvenance\":false,\"isHighlight\":false,\"isOnVie